  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0567",
      "reading_order": 751,
      "section": "1-3-2. Reference Point Adjusting Method 2",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 106.32,
        "t": 755.71466,
        "r": 392.7036239999992,
        "b": 746.8429409281769
      },
      "content": "Using the handle, determine the position at reference point."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0568",
      "reading_order": 752,
      "section": "1-3-2. Reference Point Adjusting Method 2",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 76.32,
        "t": 447.31466,
        "r": 202.04595000000003,
        "b": 438.44294092817677
      },
      "content": "Perform only in Z-axis."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0569",
      "reading_order": 753,
      "section": "1-3-2. Reference Point Adjusting Method 2",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 76.32,
        "t": 428.294696,
        "r": 319.85609999999974,
        "b": 419.42297692817675
      },
      "content": "Position X-axis at a distance from reference point."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0570",
      "reading_order": 754,
      "section": "1-3-2. Reference Point Adjusting Method 2",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 106.319658,
        "t": 391.814768,
        "r": 527.3600580000005,
        "b": 348.9231449281768
      },
      "content": "This  time,  move  the  current  position  to  be  \"C\"  value  of  Table  5-1,  set  \"EXTERNAL\" coordinate to \"0\" and then move it about 1/2 (6,000) of ball screw pitch in the opposite direction to Reference Point Return."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0571",
      "reading_order": 755,
      "section": "1-3-2. Reference Point Adjusting Method 2",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 106.32065999999999,
        "t": 340.814972,
        "r": 527.4572519999996,
        "b": 314.90324092817673
      },
      "content": "Move the reference point return dog to the position where reference point reduction signal is turned ON."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0572",
      "reading_order": 756,
      "section": "1-3-2. Reference Point Adjusting Method 2",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 106.32065999999999,
        "t": 306.795068,
        "r": 279.30193199999985,
        "b": 297.9233489281768
      },
      "content": "Reference point return the Z-axis."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0573",
      "reading_order": 757,
      "section": "1-3-2. Reference Point Adjusting Method 2",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 106.32065999999999,
        "t": 289.81517600000006,
        "r": 286.3620239999999,
        "b": 212.90364892817684
      },
      "content": "Using the handle, confirm the distance  from  reference  point  to reduction  signal  OFF  is  within  the specified range. If out of the specified, readjust the dog."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0574",
      "reading_order": 758,
      "section": "1-3-2. Reference Point Adjusting Method 2",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 106.32065999999999,
        "t": 204.795476,
        "r": 286.36202400000013,
        "b": 127.94406892817676
      },
      "content": "Perform  para.  2  and  3  again  and write the differences between \"MACHINE\"  coordinate  value  and \"C\" value of Table 5-1 at parameter 1850 as the grid shift amount."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0575",
      "reading_order": 759,
      "section": "1-3-2. Reference Point Adjusting Method 2",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 106.32065999999999,
        "t": 119.77577599999995,
        "r": 286.30390800000015,
        "b": 93.92416492817676
      },
      "content": "Turn off and  then re-apply the power."
    },
